---
description: Reconcile a queued deployment before running its bounded AI Crit
alwaysApply: false
---

<!-- pincushion-deployment-reconciliation:v2 -->

Call `get_pending_critiques` first. Keep a row with no `deploymentId` on the
legacy path; never make up deployment provenance.

For a deployment row, union its registered root/inventory with bounded rendered
same-origin, robots, and nested-sitemap discovery. If provider route hints are
absent, probe this union rather than labeling all pages changed. Reuse only local
origin-bound auth and run:

```sh
node <pincushion-mcp>/scripts/capture-snapshot.mjs --reconcile "<root-url>" "<temporary-output-dir>" --inventory=<projectPageInventory-json-or-file> --previous-receipts=<latestCaptureReceipts-json-or-file>
```

The helper performs desktop 1280×900 plus mobile 390×844 settled captures,
masks transient tiles, and writes a current-run pair for unchanged as well as
added/persistent changes during a fresh frame run.
Missing links do not remove pages; terminal 404/410 or verified out-of-scope
redirects do. Login redirects, timeout, denied access, and invalid current
evidence are inaccessible/failed, not unchanged. A committed legacy receipt
without a valid v1 fingerprint is `bootstrap_required` when current
desktop+mobile evidence is valid: stage it as `updated`. Stop on truncated discovery.

Before staging or reporting, call `register_deployment_discovered_pages` with
the exact bounded `reconciliation.discoveredPageUrls` list.
Use only returned `acceptedPendingPages` / `acceptedPageUrls`; never upload or
report a locally discovered URL that was not accepted pending.

For each accepted pending non-removed terminal result, call `record_deployment_page_result`. First stage both newly staged desktop/mobile exact capture files with `upload_page_snapshot`,
including `deploymentId`, returned-byte `contentHash`, and `captureFingerprint`;
require immutable version IDs and `staged: true`. For unchanged, the server
accepts only byte hashes exactly matching the frozen canonical pair, records
observed evidence, and discards private duplicates; use updated when either
hash differs. Only deploy-hook-frozen removed rows are excluded; do not submit
removed for an initialized local run. Inaccessible/failed results remain
truthful non-current outcomes. The backend atomically promotes staged captures
and the canonical capture report after all terminal results.
Retry an uncertain acknowledgement only with the exact same
`record_deployment_page_result` body; returned `idempotent: true` is success.

After a completed reconciliation receipt, Crit only changed/added pages and mint
an independent immutable Crit receipt. Do not call `complete_critique_request`
before reconciliation and the eligible Crit receipt are committed. The
snapshot-latest-deploy compatibility alias uses this same checkpoint and never
drains the queue independently.

For an authenticated target, supply `PINCUSHION_STORAGE_STATE` created for the
exact origin and pass `--require-auth`. Supplied or required auth that is
missing, unreadable, symlinked, non-regular, insecure, malformed, unbound,
rejected with 401/403, redirected to auth, or shown as a signed-out shell is a
hard non-success: do not stage, upload, or record it as current. Require receipt
`auth.mode: "authenticated"`; with no supplied/required state, public capture
remains `auth.mode: "anonymous"`. State contents stay local.

Create or refresh that local pair with `npx pincushion-mcp snapshot --login
"<root-url>" --proof-selector '<app-specific CSS selector visible only when
signed in>'`. The owner-only proof sidecar is bound to the exact origin and
state bytes; its selector must be visible on every authenticated route. Missing
or non-visible proof (including a neutral signed-out 200 shell) exits 6. The
initial URL and every redirect are pre-checked; a private/reserved DNS/IP answer
is rejected before navigation.

## Fresh frame run

Frame freshness is independent of `autoCritique`: call
`get_pending_deployment_frame_refreshes` even when `get_pending_critiques` is
empty. The latter controls only whether Crit is requested. Use any first
reconciliation only to discover scope—do not upload or terminalize it. Register
that bounded discovery with `register_deployment_discovered_pages`; then call
`start_deployment_capture_run`. Keep its `captureProof` only in the
authenticated MCP caller's memory—never in shell argv, a command, report, pin,
status, or file. Re-run the fresh browser pass with only the safe run ID:

```sh
node <pincushion-mcp>/scripts/capture-snapshot.mjs --reconcile "<root-url>" "<temporary-output-dir>" --capture-run-id="$CAPTURE_RUN_ID" --require-auth
```

This is `local_authenticated_agent` evidence: a trusted-executor,
local-agent-asserted capture context corroborated by uploaded bytes plus server
hash/dimension validation, not cryptographic browser attestation.

This fresh-run sequence supersedes any earlier legacy instruction to stop when
the Critique queue is empty or to record `unchanged` without a run/receipts.
Only server-confirmed historical pre-frame `not_requested` receipts retain a
legacy no-run path; never use that omission for a listed frame-refresh item.

Pass `captureRunId` and the in-memory `captureProof` only to authenticated MCP
upload/result/complete calls, never to the browser command. For every
non-removed initialized page, stage newly staged desktop/mobile images from the
current run, including unchanged. Submit their IDs and server hashes; unchanged
is accepted only when both byte hashes match the frozen canonical pair, then
the server records observed evidence and discards the duplicate private pair.
Use updated if either hash differs. Wait for server `frame_refresh_state: "completed"` (or use the guarded
`complete_deployment_capture_run`) before any Crit queue completion. A queue or
terminal reconciliation alone is never a current frame; Crit reports remain
independent immutable post-pin artifacts.
